Week 2 (Sep 21-27): Test Design and Coverage
Objective
Create professional test assets that show systematic thinking, not random clicking.

Test-design techniques
Equivalence partitioning
Boundary-value analysis
Decision-table thinking
State-transition thinking
Error guessing
Risk-based prioritization
Build your manual suite
[ ] Create 40-50 detailed test cases across registration, authentication, product search, cart, checkout, forms, and account management.
[ ] Mark 8-12 critical cases as the smoke suite.
[ ] Create a regression subset of approximately 25 high-value tests.
[ ] Include normal, invalid, blank, boundary, and state-dependent cases.
[ ] Execute the cases and record Actual Result plus Pass/Fail rather than leaving the sheet theoretical.
Recommended test-case columns
Field
Purpose
Test Case ID
Stable identifier such as TC-LOGIN-001
Feature/Scenario
What is being tested
Preconditions
Required state before execution
Steps
Numbered actions
Test Data
Inputs used
Expected Result
Observable correct behavior
Actual Result
What happened
Status
Pass / Fail / Blocked
Priority
High / Medium / Low
Notes/Evidence
Screenshot, browser, special observations

